@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
Feature: Patcher UAT
    Testing the Patcher UAT instance.

  Teardown:
    * I go to the Patcher homepage
    * I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
    * I tear down the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "${staticAccountCode}"
    * I tear down the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "${staticAccountCode}"
    * I tear down the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "${staticAccountCode}"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent3}" and type "Generated"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent3}" and type "Generated Private Public"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent4}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent5}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent6}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent7}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent8}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent9}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent10}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent11}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent12}" and type "Rebase"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent4}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent5}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent6}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent7}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent8}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent9}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent10}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent11}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent12}" and type "Workaround"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent4}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent5}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent6}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent7}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent8}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent9}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent10}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent11}" and type "Patch"
    * I tear down the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent12}" and type "Patch"

  Scenario: Create a 72 build
    @priority = "5"
    As a TSE, I should be able to create a 7.1 build containing private child builds
    Given I log into the Patcher homepage as the admin user
    And I generate random fix content for the first fix
    And I generate random fix content for the second fix
    And I generate random fix content for the third fix
    And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
      | Product         | DXP 7.2                                                         |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210                                              |
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent1}                                            |
      | Branch Name     | LPP-34242                                                       |
      | Github URL      | git@github.com:Liferay-Patcher-Test-Fixes/liferay-portal-ee.git |
    And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
      | Product         | DXP 7.2                                                         |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210                                              |
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent2}                                            |
      | Branch Name     | LPS-108761_base                                                 |
      | Github URL      | git@github.com:Liferay-Patcher-Test-Fixes/liferay-portal-ee.git |
    And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
      | Product         | DXP 7.2                                                         |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210                                              |
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent3}                                            |
      | Branch Name     | fpf1-168475534                                                  |
      | Github URL      | git@github.com:Liferay-Patcher-Test-Fixes/liferay-portal-ee.git |
    And I wait for "5" seconds
    Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent1} |
      | Version         | 1.0                  |
      | Product         | DXP 7.2              |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210   |
      | Patcher Status  | Adding               |
      | Type            | Patch                |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent2} |
      | Version         | 1.0                  |
      | Product         | DXP 7.2              |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210   |
      | Patcher Status  | Adding               |
      | Type            | Patch                |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent3} |
      | Version         | 1.0                  |
      | Product         | DXP 7.2              |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210   |
      | Patcher Status  | Adding               |
      | Type            | Patch                |
    When I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" for add completion
    And I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Patch" for add completion
    And I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch" for add completion
    Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent1}       |
      | Version         | 1.0                        |
      | Product         | DXP 7.2                    |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210         |
      | Git Hash        | bcb7100e49                 |
      | Patcher Status  | Complete                   |
      | Type            | Patch                      |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat) |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent2}       |
      | Version         | 1.0                        |
      | Product         | DXP 7.2                    |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210         |
      | Git Hash        | d5ffd78e62                 |
      | Patcher Status  | Complete                   |
      | Type            | Patch                      |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat) |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent3}       |
      | Version         | 1.0                        |
      | Product         | DXP 7.2                    |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210         |
      | Git Hash        | 17d30328d3                 |
      | Patcher Status  | Complete                   |
      | Type            | Patch                      |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat) |
    When I generate a random ticket number
    And I create a Patcher build for a new account with the following values
      | Product         | DXP 7.2                                                        |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210                                             |
      | Tickets List    | ${staticFixContent1},${staticFixContent2},${staticFixContent3} |
      | Account Code    | STVINTRA                                                       |
      | Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber}                                          |
    And I set the account code "STVINTRA" as a static variable
    And I wait for "5" seconds
    Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
      | Type            | Official                |
      | Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber}   |
      | Version         | 1.0                     |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210      |
      | Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 3 Tickets |
      | Patcher Status  | Merging                 |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
      | Version         | 1.0                                                              |
      | Name            | ${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3} |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210                                               |
      | Patcher Status  | Merging Only                                                     |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent1}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
      | Name     | ${staticFixContent1} |
      | Version  | 1.0                  |
      | Git Hash | bcb7100e49           |
      | Status   | Complete             |
      | Type     | Patch                |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent2}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
      | Name     | ${staticFixContent2} |
      | Version  | 1.0                  |
      | Git Hash | d5ffd78e62           |
      | Status   | Complete             |
      | Type     | Patch                |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent3}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
      | Name     | ${staticFixContent3} |
      | Version  | 1.0                  |
      | Git Hash | 17d30328d3           |
      | Status   | Complete             |
      | Type     | Patch                |
    When I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" for merge completion
    And I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" for compile completion using the "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat)" Jenkins job
    Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
      | Type            | Official                       |
      | Support Ticket  | ${staticTicketNumber}          |
      | Version         | 1.0                            |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210             |
      | Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 3 Tickets        |
      | Patcher Status  | Complete                       |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat) |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)     |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticTicketNumber}" on the account "STVINTRA" with the following values
      | Version         | 1.0                                                              |
      | Name            | ${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3} |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-base-7210                                               |
      | Patcher Status  | Complete Merging Only                                            |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)                                       |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat)                                   |

  Scenario: Create a 71 build with public child build and change the status to ready for release
    @priority = "3"
    As a TSE, I should be able to create and release a 7.1 build that contains a public child build
    Given I log into the Patcher homepage as the admin user
    And I generate random fix content for the first fix
    And I generate random fix content for the second fix
    And I generate random fix content for the third fix
    And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
      | Product         | DXP 7.1                                                         |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110                                             |
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent1}                                            |
      | Branch Name     | LPS-91660-DXP-7                                                 |
      | Github URL      | git@github.com:Liferay-Patcher-Test-Fixes/liferay-portal-ee.git |
    And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
      | Product         | DXP 7.1                                                         |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110                                             |
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent2}                                            |
      | Branch Name     | LPS-108761_DXP-7                                                |
      | Github URL      | git@github.com:Liferay-Patcher-Test-Fixes/liferay-portal-ee.git |
    And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
      | Product         | DXP 7.1                                                         |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-6-7110                                             |
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent3}                                            |
      | Branch Name     | LPS-113733-fix-pack-dxp-6-7110                                  |
      | Github URL      | git@github.com:Liferay-Patcher-Test-Fixes/liferay-portal-ee.git |
    And I wait for "5" seconds
    Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent1} |
      | Version         | 1.0                  |
      | Product         | DXP 7.1              |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110  |
      | Patcher Status  | Adding               |
      | Type            | Patch                |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent2} |
      | Version         | 1.0                  |
      | Product         | DXP 7.1              |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110  |
      | Patcher Status  | Adding               |
      | Type            | Patch                |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent3} |
      | Version         | 1.0                  |
      | Product         | DXP 7.1              |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-6-7110  |
      | Patcher Status  | Adding               |
      | Type            | Patch                |
    When I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" for add completion
    And I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Patch" for add completion
    And I check the Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch" for add completion
    Then I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent1}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent1}       |
      | Version         | 1.0                        |
      | Product         | DXP 7.1                    |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110        |
      | Git Hash        | 1916d4cf71                 |
      | Patcher Status  | Complete                   |
      | Type            | Patch                      |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat) |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent2}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent2}       |
      | Version         | 1.0                        |
      | Product         | DXP 7.1                    |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110        |
      | Git Hash        | d94a1b18e1                 |
      | Patcher Status  | Complete                   |
      | Type            | Patch                      |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat) |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher fix containing the content "${staticFixContent3}" and type "Patch" with the following values
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent3}       |
      | Version         | 1.0                        |
      | Product         | DXP 7.1                    |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-6-7110        |
      | Git Hash        | 0d085a8a96                 |
      | Patcher Status  | Complete                   |
      | Type            | Patch                      |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat) |
    When I create a request as a user with the email address "no-reply@intuitive.com.broken" with the following values
      | Product           | prd_liferay_dxp_7_1                              |
      | Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
      | System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
      | Subject           | Patcher Request Subject                          |
      | Description       | Patcher Request Description                      |
      | Organization Name | Intuitive Surgical-EE-IT                         |
    And I create a Patcher build for a new account with the following values
      | Product         | DXP 7.1                                                        |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110                                            |
      | Tickets List    | ${staticFixContent1},${staticFixContent2},${staticFixContent3} |
      | Account Code    | INTUITIVE                                                      |
      | Support Ticket  | ${staticRequestIdList}                                         |
    And I set the account code "INTUITIVE" as a static variable
    And I wait for "5" seconds
    Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
      | Type            | Official                |
      | Support Ticket  | ${staticRequestIdList}  |
      | Version         | 1.0                     |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110     |
      | Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 3 Tickets |
      | Patcher Status  | Rebasing                |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
      | Version         | 1.0                                                              |
      | Name            | ${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3} |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110                                              |
      | Patcher Status  | Rebasing Merging Only                                            |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent1}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
      | Name     | ${staticFixContent1} |
      | Version  | 1.0                  |
      | Git Hash | 1916d4cf71           |
      | Status   | Complete             |
      | Type     | Patch                |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent2}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
      | Name     | ${staticFixContent2} |
      | Version  | 1.0                  |
      | Git Hash | d94a1b18e1           |
      | Status   | Complete             |
      | Type     | Patch                |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher child build fix with the name "${staticFixContent3}" for the child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
      | Name    | ${staticFixContent3} |
      | Version | 1.0                  |
      | Status  | Complete             |
      | Type    | Rebase               |
    When I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" for rebase completion
    And I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" for merge completion
    And I check the Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" for compile completion using the "fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat)" Jenkins job
    Then I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
      | Type            | Official                       |
      | Support Ticket  | ${staticRequestIdList}         |
      | Version         | 1.0                            |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110            |
      | Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 3 Tickets        |
      | Patcher Status  | Complete                       |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat) |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)     |
    And I should be able to view a Patcher child build with the name "${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3}" for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
      | Version         | 1.0                                                              |
      | Name            | ${staticFixContent1}, ${staticFixContent2}, ${staticFixContent3} |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110                                              |
      | Patcher Status  | Complete Merging Only                                            |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat)                                   |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)                                       |
    When I change a Patcher build status to ready for release for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE"
    Then the ticket with the ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should not have the comment containing the text "liferay-hotfix-"
    And the ticket with the ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should not have the comment containing the text "-7110.zip"
    And I should be able to view a Patcher build for the ticket "${staticRequestIdList}" on the account "INTUITIVE" with the following values
      | Type            | Official                       |
      | Support Ticket  |${staticRequestIdList}          |
      | Version         | 1.0                            |
      | Project Version | fix-pack-dxp-7-7110            |
      | Content         | 0 Fix Packs + 3 Tickets        |
      | Patcher Status  | Ready for Release              |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-hotfix-7x(uat) |
      | Jenkins         | fixpack-builder-agent(uat)     |

  Scenario: Create a public MP build
    @priority = "4"
    As a TSE, I should be able to create a public MP build
    Given I log into the Patcher homepage as the admin user
    And I generate random fix content for the first fix
    And I generate random fix content for the second fix
    And I generate random fix content for the third fix
    And I generate random fix content for the fourth fix
    And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
      | Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base                                  |
      | Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010                           |
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent1}                                            |
      | Branch Name     | LPS-87103                                                       |
      | Github URL      | git@github.com:Liferay-Patcher-Test-Fixes/liferay-portal-ee.git |
    And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
      | Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base                                  |
      | Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010                           |
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent2}                                            |
      | Branch Name     | LPP-32185-hotfix                                                |
      | Github URL      | git@github.com:Liferay-Patcher-Test-Fixes/liferay-portal-ee.git |
      | Workaround      | true                                                            |
    And I create a Patcher fix with the following values
      | Product         | DXP 7.0 Liferay Knowledge Base                                  |
      | Project Version | marketplace-knowledge-base-3.0.2-7010                           |
      | Content         | ${staticFixContent3}                                            |
